  <reporting-org ref="US-GOV-9" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Department of the Interior</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">AFRICAN ELEPHANT CONSERVATION GENETICS III</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE PURPOSE OF THIS PROJECT IS TO SUPPORT A RANGE-WIDE ELEPHANT CONSERVATION EFFORT, WITH A FOCUS ON WEST AND CENTRAL AFRICA BY IMPROVING AFRICAN ELEPHANT GENETICS RESEARCH AND STRENGTHENING THE CAPACITY OF AFRICAN RESEARCH INSTITUTIONS. THIS PROJECT IS INTENDED TO CONSERVE AFRICAN FOREST AND SAVANNA ELEPHANTS AND THEIR HABITAT BY ADDRESSING THE IMPACTS OF EXISTING GENETICS RESEARCH GAPS AND SUPPORTING EVIDENCE-BASED DECISION MAKING BY CONSERVATION MANAGERS. SPECIFIC ACTIVITIES INCLUDE: (1) CONDUCTING GENOMIC SEQUENCING OF FOREST ELEPHANTS AND ANALYSIS OF WEST VERSUS CENTRAL AFRICAN FOREST ELEPHANTS TO DETERMINE THE DEGREE OF GENETIC DISTINCTIVENESS (2) CONDUCTING GENOMIC ASSESSMENT OF ELEPHANTS AT THE EXTREMES OF THEIR RANGE TO DETERMINE GENETICALLY DISTINCT POPULATIONS WORTHY OF SEPARATE CONSERVATION PLANS (3) TESTING A NOVEL ELEPHANT DUNG DNA COLLECTION METHOD WITH GENSAVER CARDS (4) EXPANDING THE CAPABILITIES OF THE LOXODONTA LOCALIZER SOFTWARE TOOL AND (5) PROVIDING CAPACITY DEVELOPMENT SUPPORT FOR AFRICAN ELEPHANT RANGE COUNTRY LABORATORIES.</narrative>
  </description>
